If you call `recover` here, the panic will be recovered here, which is not we want.
Suggest just check `closed`.

```go
defer func() {
    // close if panic happens
    if !closed { e.analyzeExec.Close() }
}()

Suggest,

```go
func (e *EExplainExec) generateExplainInfo(ctx context.Context) (result [][]string, err error) {
...

var nextErr, closeErr error
defer func() 
    closeErr = e.analyzeExec.Close()
    	if nextErr != nil {
			if closeErr != nil {
				err = errors.New(nextErr.Error() + ", " + closeErr.Error())
			} else {
				err =nextErr
			}
		} else {
                err = closeErr
        }
}
...    
}
```
